    "case_id": "452",
    "case_summary": "A 39-year-old woman with no other significant medical history presented with intractable mucocutaneous lesions that had been evolving for 10 years. No swollen cervical and axillary lymph nodes were palpable.\n\nSmall bullae, erosions, and crusts were present on the lower lip. Erosions with epithelized mucosa were observed in the oral cavity. Flaccid discrete and coalesced bullae, crusts, and erosions over erythematous and cicatricial lesions were present on the face, trunk, and extremities.\n\n{'Imaging Studies': 'Chest, abdomen, and pelvic computed tomography showed no abnormalities.', 'Endoscopic Procedures': 'Gastrointestinal endoscopy and colonoscopy results identified no abnormalities.', 'Histopathology': 'Skin biopsy revealed spongiosis and numerous neutrophils with nuclear dust in the epidermis and superficial perivascular dermatitis with predominant infiltration of lymphocytes in the dermis.', 'Immunological Studies': ['Direct immunofluorescence (IF): No obvious deposits of IgG, IgA, and C3 to either the epithelial cell surface or the basement membrane zone', 'Indirect IF using normal human skin and 1-molar sodium chloride–split normal human skin: No IgG and IgA antibodies', 'Indirect IF using rat bladder: Negative results', 'Chemiluminescent enzyme immunoassays: Negative for Dsg1, Dsg3, and BP180 16th noncollagenous domain', 'Enzyme-linked immunosorbent assays: Negative for BP230, type VII collagen, and desmocollins 1 to 3', 'Immunoblotting of normal human epidermal extract: Positive for IgG autoantibodies to envoplakin (210 kDa) and periplakin (190 kDa)'], 'Images': {'Figure A': 'Clinical findings on the lower lip', 'Figure B': 'Clinical findings on oral mucosa', 'Figure C and D': 'Clinical findings on the back and buttock', 'Figure E and F': 'Histopathological features (hematoxylin and eosin staining)', 'Figure G': 'Results of immunoblotting of normal human epidermal extract'}}",
    "frontier": [
      "B1",
      "B2",
      "B3"
    ],
    "root": {
